  "2026-10-02T22:04:43.087Z","harness:codex","Review alignment: the existing negative-controls criterion now explicitly includes confident completion despite unresolved assertions and requires failure of the corresponding future conflicting-assertions oracle. This is a queued acceptance-plan correction, not a claim that the new scenario family has been implemented; the feature remains open and unclaimed."
body: "## Outcome and ownership\nChild of #1357. Measure whether the delivered context lets an agent choose the correct safe action, including when it should abstain, rather than relying on retrieval ranking as a proxy.\n\nExtend [pm-atfm](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/blob/main/.agents/pm/features/pm-atfm.toon) and the existing #863 [tokens-per-task owner pm-g3n00m](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/blob/main/.agents/pm/stories/pm-g3n00m.toon). Retrieval evaluation and token accounting already exist. Retain them; add decision-level scenarios and outcome evidence.\n\n## Implementation plan\n1. Add a versioned scenario schema with deterministic seed/clock, initial workspace, intervening events, actor scope, required evidence/categories, permitted next actions, expected abstention/insufficient-context outcomes and terminal success criteria.\n2. Start with deterministic SDK reference-policy checks so CI remains offline and reproducible. An optional model-driven evaluator is separately versioned, records model/configuration and repeated-run uncertainty, and cannot hide deterministic invariant failures.\n3. Add six mandatory scenario families: changed decision; conflicting assertions; expired evidence; interrupted execution with unknown/completed effects; missing mandatory context under budget; and cross-scope retrieval/cache contamination. Include both safe-success and correct-abstention cases for each applicable family.\n4. Evaluate the consumer-visible emitted context and action trace, not inaccessible oracle/source state. The oracle scores results; it must not leak expected answers into the agent input.\n5. Report decision correctness, unsafe-action count, unsupported-claim rate, coverage/sufficiency accuracy, abstention precision/recall, terminal task success, artifact/effect correctness, latency and delivered token cost. Publish task-success-per-token alongside raw success and tokens, with explicit zero-token/zero-success handling.\n6. Integrate existing accounting across the full task trajectory: orientation, retries, refreshes, failures and resume. State whether tokens are measured or estimated and whether agent/provider tokens are included. Keep stratified per-scenario results so an aggregate cannot hide a safety failure.\n7. Add an unchanged-baseline path, documented review/update procedure, minimum case counts and executable negative controls. Preserve existing retrieval/quality/performance gates.\n\n## Acceptance and tests\n- [ ] Changed/superseded decisions change the expected action; stale evidence requires refresh or abstention\n- [ ] Unresolved conflicts and omitted mandatory context cannot pass as confident correct completion\n- [ ] Resume after a confirmed effect does not repeat it; unknown effects require reconciliation\n- [ ] Cross-scope hidden data never improves a score through unauthorized access\n- [ ] A shorter context that drops required evidence fails correctness even if its token count improves\n- [ ] Every mandatory family has nonempty fixtures and independently meaningful pass/fail thresholds\n- [ ] Negative controls deliberately choose the obsolete decision, confidently complete despite an unresolved assertion conflict, ignore expiry, replay an effect, omit a category and leak scope; each fails its corresponding gate, including the conflicting-assertions gate\n- [ ] Fixed seeds and clocks yield stable deterministic results; optional model evaluation reports variance and configuration\n- [ ] Packed public SDK and CLI/MCP runs consume the same scenario contracts and final output receipts\n- [ ] Documentation includes how to add cases, interpret abstention and update reviewed baselines without weakening safety floors\n\n## Dependencies and rollout\nDefine fixtures before implementation; add contract-level cases as the temporal, coverage, checkpoint and policy children of #1357 land. Gate deterministic safety invariants immediately; establish cost baselines before setting improvement targets. No invented percentage win or deadline.\n\n## Non-goals\nNo second retrieval harness, optimization of nDCG alone, rewarding universal abstention, rewarding truncation as efficiency, or treating an LLM judge as the sole correctness authority.\n\n## Linked implementation slices\n- Verifies #1358, #1361, #1359 and #1360\n- Scenario schema and fixtures can land first; feature-specific acceptance gates activate as their contracts become available"
